{number: 67}
{title: Pass Me Not, O Gentle Savior}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] Pass me not, O gentle Savior,
[Db] Hear my humble [Ab] cry;
While on others Thou art calling,
[Eb7] Do not pass me [Ab] by.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Ab] Savior, Savior,
[Db] Hear my humble [Ab] cry;
While on others Thou art calling,
[Eb7] Do not pass me [Ab] by.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] Let me at a throne of mercy
[Db] Find a sweet re-[Ab] lief;
Kneeling there in deep contrition,
[Eb7] Help my unbe-[Ab] lief.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Ab] Trusting only in Thy merit,
[Db] Would I seek Thy [Ab] face;
Heal my wounded, broken spirit,
[Eb7] Save me by Thy [Ab] grace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Ab] Thou the Spring of all my comfort,
[Db] More than life to [Ab] me,
Whom have I on earth beside Thee?
[Eb7] Whom in heav'n but [Ab] Thee?
{end_of_verse}
